\begin_layout Standard
The model consists of two main blocks namely the Aircraft Model and Nonlinear
 RBD.
 The Nonlinear RBD block calculates the 16 States necessary for the Aircraft
 Model to function which calculates the delta forces and moments and feeds
 them back to the Nonlinear Rigid Body Dynamics block creating a loop that
 simulates the aircraft.
 The whole Simulink model takes pilots input signals ( 
\begin_inset Formula $\delta$
\end_inset

aileron , 
\begin_inset Formula $\delta$
\end_inset

rudder , 
\begin_inset Formula $\delta$
\end_inset

elevator , 
\begin_inset Formula $\delta$
\end_inset

thrust ) as input and gives out many variables as output to determine the
 aircraft performance.
\end_layout

