\begin_layout Standard
The Model gives out Position (
\begin_inset Formula $x,y,z)$
\end_inset

, Euler angles (
\begin_inset Formula $\phi,\theta,\psi x$
\end_inset

), Velocities (
\begin_inset Formula $u,v,w$
\end_inset

), Angular Velocities (
\begin_inset Formula $p,q,r$
\end_inset

), and both angle of attack (
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha$
\end_inset

) and Side-slip angle (
\begin_inset Formula $\beta$
\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Rigid Body Dynamics block uses Euler 6 DOF Block to calculate the 16
 States.
 It takes forces and moments as input, The input forces are a result of
 Delta forces (
\begin_inset Formula $\Delta F$
\end_inset

) coming from the Aircraft model plus the gravity contribution in the body
 axis plus the gravity contribution after Euler angles change.
 Then the states are sent to the Aircraft Model.
\end_layout

